# PA-4 baseline: delegation and workflow execution

**Snapshot:** Nexus `0151bef3a8a95e3cd3df2d632439b30811e6415c` (`origin/main`), inspected 2026-11-21. This is a source and test inventory; source presence and test-file names are not runtime verification, and the existing tests listed here were not run for this baseline.

| Area | Status | Evidence and observed boundary |
|---|---|---|
| Interactive turns and inference | Implemented | `AutonomousAgent.runTurn` delegates to `runTurnImpl` ([agent.ts:4186](../../cli/src/agent.ts#L4186), [run_turn.ts:26](../../cli/src/core/run_turn.ts#L26)); provider recovery and context admission are in the turn path. `TurnResult` distinguishes interrupted, blocked and failed executions and requires evidence for verified outcomes ([turn.ts:17](../../cli/src/core/turn.ts#L17), [turn.ts:423](../../cli/src/core/turn.ts#L423)). |
| Transient delegation | Partially implemented; qualification pending | `runSubagent` remains the in-turn child path ([agent.ts](../../cli/src/agent.ts)); `spawn_subagent` now selects a predefined profile, narrows tools at schema and dispatcher boundaries, clears inherited full access, and emits a typed receipt ([spine_handlers.ts](../../cli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts), [dispatch_tool_call.ts](../../cli/src/core/dispatch_tool_call.ts)). Prompt-only calls default to read-only `semantic_explorer`; writable profiles require an established worktree. Depth and per-parent child-attempt limits are enforced. Process-wide resource budgets, full task/session/workspace grant derivation, deterministic security tests, and independent evidence review remain outstanding; see [transient authority milestone](PA4_TRANSIENT_AUTHORITY.md).
| Durable work units and scheduling | Implemented | `newOperation` constructs operation state ([operation.ts:502](../../cli/src/core/operation.ts#L502)) and the graph rejects dependency cycles ([operation.ts:582](../../cli/src/core/operation.ts#L582)); `ConvergenceScheduler` selects transitions ([scheduler.ts:53](../../cli/src/core/scheduler.ts#L53)); `driveOperation` and `OperationStore` persist and resume work ([operation_runner.ts:717](../../cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts#L717), [operation_runner_persistence.ts:28](../../cli/src/core/operation_runner_persistence.ts#L28)). Existing tests cover schema, restart, concurrency and isolated integration.
| Roles and independent review | Implemented, incomplete | Specialist profiles define permitted tools, read-only declarations, inputs, ceilings and output contracts ([specialist_profiles.ts:22](../../cli/src/core/specialist_profiles.ts#L22)); operation roles include team and specialist profiles ([roles.ts:101](../../cli/src/core/roles.ts#L101)). Independent-review formatting and verdict validation exist ([independent_review.ts:131](../../cli/src/core/independent_review.ts#L131), [independent_review.ts:204](../../cli/src/core/independent_review.ts#L204)); source presence does not establish all requested independence dimensions or reviewer behavior under truncated evidence.
| Resource and provider handling | Implemented, incomplete | `ResourceRegistry` handles eligibility and provider conditions ([resources.ts:194](../../cli/src/core/resources.ts#L194)); provider capability states include `unknown` and `unavailable` ([provider_capabilities.ts:26](../../cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts#L26)); recovery classification/controller exists ([provider_recovery.ts:96](../../cli/src/core/provider_recovery.ts#L96), [provider_recovery.ts:367](../../cli/src/core/provider_recovery.ts#L367)). Provider test sources include `provider_wire_matrix.test.ts`, `provider_capabilities.test.ts`, `provider_robustness.test.ts`, `cloud_providers.test.ts` and `provider_recovery.test.ts`; this assignment's complete workflow has not been run against the requested minimal contract fixture.
| `/team` and operation CLI | Implemented, incomplete | `TeamOrchestrator` maps roles to durable work units ([team.ts:43](../../cli/src/team.ts#L43), [team.ts:126](../../cli/src/team.ts#L126)); the operation CLI accepts validated JSON work-unit specs ([operation_cli.ts:106](../../cli/src/operation_cli.ts#L106)). The REPL has a dedicated `/team` handler ([repl.ts:1702](../../cli/src/repl.ts#L1702)); the sidecar routes commands through a separate slash router ([router.ts:14](../../cli/src/slash/router.ts#L14)). TUI completion/help comes from the slash catalogue ([catalog.ts:138](../../cli/src/slash/catalog.ts#L138)), with remote invocation parsing in Rust ([slash.rs:25](../../core/src/bin/nexus_tui/slash.rs#L25)).
| `/loop`, `/goal`, `/batch` | `/batch` implemented, `/loop` and `/goal` unimplemented | `/batch` is present in the command catalogue and routes to `BatchOrchestrator`; it validates existing operation JSON specs and persists through `OperationStore` and `OperationRunner` ([batch.ts](../../cli/src/batch.ts), [batch_spec.ts](../../cli/src/batch_spec.ts), [router.ts](../../cli/src/slash/router.ts), [repl.ts](../../cli/src/repl.ts)). `batch.test.ts` and `batch_spec.test.ts` cover command behavior. `/loop` and `/goal` lifecycle controllers remain absent; loop detector tests do not implement durable loop state, and the objective ledger has no `/goal` lifecycle.
| Pause, cancellation and restart | Implemented, incomplete | Durable operations include distinct `PAUSED`, cancellation and bounded restart reconciliation ([operation.ts](../../cli/src/core/operation.ts), [operation_runner.ts](../../cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts), [operation_cli.ts](../../cli/src/operation_cli.ts)). `/batch` pause is honored at a safe boundary. Unknown effects still need stronger reconciliation semantics for the broader delegation assignment; `/loop` lifecycle recovery is absent.
| Skills and authority | Implemented, incomplete | Skill activation has constraints and content digests ([skill_activation.ts:67](../../cli/src/core/skill_activation.ts#L67), [skill_activation.ts:104](../../cli/src/core/skill_activation.ts#L104)). Capability registration exists ([capabilities.ts:120](../../cli/src/core/capabilities.ts#L120)) and the orchestration capability schema declares `spawn_subagent` ([orchestration.ts:38](../../cli/src/core/capability_definitions/orchestration.ts#L38)). Full effect-path mediation and path-scoped profile/skill eligibility still require adversarial tests from the assignment.

## Roadmap and compatibility notes

- v1.3 PA-1, PA-2 and PA-3 already cover parallel visibility, verified integration and goal semantics. PA-4 stages this assignment against those units and the active WP-P10-02 durable-budget work.
- Operation records are versioned and reject records from a newer schema ([operation_schema.ts](../../cli/src/core/operation_schema.ts)). PA-1 resource reservations use schema v4; old records remain readable and schedule serially when their prior parallel declarations lack reservations.
- XERJ definition-first lookup identified `TeamOrchestrator`, `WorkUnitSpec`, `newOperation` and the existing dependency-cycle check. The first batch-spec package reuses the operation parser and constructor; no orchestration code was copied.
- No provider, gateway, or homelab-ai change is part of the workstream.

## Implementation progress (2026-11-21)

